time=2026-10-26T23:20:01.234Z level=INFO msg="model prompt" record=prov-2026-0906216b attempt=1 prompt="## The change\n\nthe migrationAgree function reports whether a staged file differs from its base only in the opening lines of its sedum regions, comparing the text outside regions and the identity, opening-line prefix, body and closing line of each region.\n\n## Constraints on it\n\n- The function receives the base content and the staged content, both strings, in that order\n- The function returns a boolean\n- The function splits each content with splitRegions (regen_run.go; parameter: a string; returns the outside text string, a slice of regionMarker and a boolean that is false when malformed)\n- The function returns false when either content is malformed\n- The function returns false when the base content has no region\n- The function returns false when the outside texts differ in any byte\n- The function returns false when the two marker slices differ in length\n- The function returns false when any pair of markers at the same position differs in Prefix\n- The function returns false when any pair of markers at the same position differs in Close\n- Everything in an opening line after its Prefix, other than the tier, record, gen and pkg values, may differ\n- regionMarker is the struct declared in regen_run.go with the string fields Tier, Record, Gen, Pkg, Prefix, Body and Close\n- The function returns false when any pair of markers at the same position differs in Tier\n- The function returns false when any pair of markers at the same position differs in Record\n- The function returns false when any pair of markers at the same position differs in Gen\n- The function returns false when any pair of markers at the same position differs in Pkg\n- The function returns false when any pair of markers at the same position differs in Body\n- Otherwise the function returns true\n- The function adds no imports\n\n## Supplementary context\n\nThis section is supplied by the caller, not by the record. It is advisory: it does not add to or change what the record authorized, and the files below remain the only ones the actions may reach.\n\nCaller notes:\n\nSelect the single setFunction invocation for migrationAgree in cmd/provenance/migration_run.go. regionMarker (regen_run.go) now has the string fields Tier, Record, Gen, Pkg, Prefix, Body and Close; compare every one of them at each position as the record's constraints say (Prefix, Close, Tier, Record, Gen, Pkg and Body each make the function return false when they differ). Select no addImport.\n\nSelections made for this change on an earlier run (context only; they are not applied):\n\n- {\"action\":\"setFunction\",\"kwargs\":{\"code\":\"func migrationAgree(base, staged string) bool {\\n\\tbaseOutside, baseMarkers, ok := splitRegions(base)\\n\\tif !ok {\\n\\t\\treturn false\\n\\t}\\n\\tif len(baseMarkers) == 0 {\\n\\t\\treturn false\\n\\t}\\n\\tstagedOutside, stagedMarkers, ok := splitRegions(staged)\\n\\tif !ok {\\n\\t\\treturn false\\n\\t}\\n\\tif baseOutside != stagedOutside {\\n\\t\\treturn false\\n\\t}\\n\\tif len(baseMarkers) != len(stagedMarkers) {\\n\\t\\treturn false\\n\\t}\\n\\tfor i := range baseMarkers {\\n\\t\\tb := baseMarkers[i]\\n\\t\\ts := stagedMarkers[i]\\n\\t\\tif b.Tier != s.Tier || b.Record != s.Record || b.Gen != s.Gen {\\n\\t\\t\\treturn false\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t}\\n\\treturn true\\n}\",\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/migration_run.go\",\"name\":\"migrationAgree\"}}\n\n## Already present\n\nThese regions already exist in the files below and belong to other changes. Do not select them: an action that resolves to one of them would conflict with the change that owns it.\n\n- cmd/provenance/migration_run.go: addImport {\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/migration_run.go\",\"path\":\"os\"} (owned by prov-2026-6b30af71; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/migration_run.go: addImport {\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/migration_run.go\",\"path\":\"os/exec\"} (owned by prov-2026-6b30af71; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/migration_run.go: addImport {\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/migration_run.go\",\"path\":\"path/filepath\"} (owned by prov-2026-6b30af71; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/migration_run.go: addImport {\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/migration_run.go\",\"path\":\"strings\"} (owned by prov-2026-6b30af71; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/migration_run.go: addImport {\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/migration_run.go\",\"path\":\"github.com/livecodelife/provenance/scope\"} (owned by prov-2026-ea383d6a; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/migration_run.go: setFunction {\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/migration_run.go\",\"name\":\"exportBase\"} (owned by prov-2026-1b5e1e6e; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/migration_run.go: setFunction {\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/migration_run.go\",\"name\":\"classesUnchanged\"} (owned by prov-2026-3cc00a7b; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/migration_run.go: setFunction {\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/migration_run.go\",\"name\":\"recordClasses\"} (owned by prov-2026-6b30af71; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/migration_run.go: setFunction {\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/migration_run.go\",\"name\":\"pureMigration\"} (owned by prov-2026-ea383d6a; do not select)\n\n## Files\n\nThese files exist and are the only ones the actions below may reach:\n\n- cmd/provenance/migration_run.go (package go; injection points: decls, imports)\n\n## Actions\n\n{\n  \"actions\": [\n    {\n      \"action\": \"addImport\",\n      \"package\": \"go\",\n      \"description\": \"Imports one package.\",\n      \"kwargs\": {\n        \"file\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"required\": true,\n          \"description\": \"The Go file to write into. It must be one of the authorized files.\"\n        },\n        \"path\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"required\": true,\n          \"description\": \"The import path.\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"anchor\": [\n        \"imports\"\n      ],\n      \"requires\": [\n        \"path\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\